## Layers

- `raw/` — immutable source files. The source of truth. **Never edit or delete these.** Read from them only.
- `raw/assets/` — images downloaded from sources, referenced locally.
- `wiki/` — markdown you own entirely. Create and update freely.
- `AGENTS.md` (this file) — the rulebook. Co-evolve it with the user when conventions change.

## Wiki layout

- `wiki/index.md` — content catalog. Update on every ingest. Keep exactly one `index.md`, directly under `wiki/` — never create a same-named page in a subdirectory.
- `wiki/log.md` — append-only timeline. Append on every ingest, filed-back answer, and lint pass. Keep exactly one `log.md`, directly under `wiki/` — never create a same-named page in a subdirectory.
- `wiki/overview.md` — top-level synthesis and entry point.
- `wiki/sources/` — one summary page per ingested source.
- `wiki/entities/` — people, organizations, products, places, works.
- `wiki/concepts/` — ideas, themes, topics, methods.

## Page conventions

- One entity / concept / source per file. Filenames in kebab-case.
- Cross-reference with `[[wikilinks]]` so Obsidian's graph view connects pages. Link liberally.
- Every wiki page starts with YAML frontmatter:

```yaml
---
title: <human title>
type: source | entity | concept | overview
created: YYYY-MM-DD
updated: YYYY-MM-DD
sources: [<source-page-slugs>]
tags: []
---
```

- Cite claims back to the `sources/` page they came from. Source pages link to the file in `raw/`.

## New page vs. edit existing

Create a new page when a distinct entity or concept recurs across sources or earns its own identity. Otherwise fold the detail into an existing page and add a cross-reference. Early on, prefer fewer, richer pages; split a section into its own page when it outgrows its host.

## Workflows

**Ingest** — when the user adds a source: read it, discuss key takeaways, write a `sources/` summary, update `index.md`, update every relevant entity/concept page, flag contradictions with existing claims, append a `log.md` entry. A single source may touch 10–15 pages.

**Query** — when the user asks a question: read `index.md`, drill into relevant pages, answer with citations. If the answer is durable (a comparison, analysis, or discovered connection), file it back as a new wiki page so explorations compound.

**Lint** — periodically: find contradictions, stale claims, orphan pages, missing cross-references, concepts mentioned but lacking a page, and gaps a web search could fill. Report and propose fixes.

## Log format

Each `log.md` entry starts with a parseable prefix so `grep "^## \[" log.md | tail` works:

```
## [YYYY-MM-DD] ingest | <source title>
## [YYYY-MM-DD] query  | <question, filed back as [[page]]>
## [YYYY-MM-DD] lint   | <summary of findings>
```

